SUMMARY:UnRavel yo’self at Lower Big Hungry Falls
DESCRIPTION:Hendo Fun Friends\n**We are the Sloth Hiking Group: “We will
  get there when we get there.” We dare to go where the ‘real’ hike g
 roups don’t !!**\n**This is a designated ‘silent’ Meditation Hike\; 
 we will engage quiet at the falls. But "Ooh's and Aah's" are encouraged. 
 ”**\n**https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=TQ8H4EK2vt4**\nI am going to unra
 vel my stress at Lower Big Hungry Falls. Up to 12 ppl are welcome to join 
 me.\nI will spend up to 3 hours at the falls swimming\, eating\, reading\,
  ponderin’ and pretending to meditate. (shorter durations optional)\n**W
 e are also doing lite clean-up maintenance.**\n**Hike Details:**\nLength: 
 1.1 mi RT (in&out)\; **Total descent: 325 ft (and return)**\nDifficulty: N
 atural trail w/ rock & roots.\nDrive time: 20 min\n**Return Not earlier th
 an:** 2:30 PM\nCarpool contributions appreciated. $2.00 suggested\nWeather
  Check: Hendersonville\nWAITLISTED PEOPLE WILL BE ADDED AS DRIVERS SIGN ON
 .\n(I currently have 2.5 driver(s). (=9ppl)\nWe suggest masks and open win
 dows while carpooling. Only you know your own health status so judge accor
 dingly if an event may endanger your health or the health of others.\nPlea
 se bring an extra pair of shoes to avoid bringing your muddy shoes into th
 e driver's car at the end of the hike.\nIncessant prattlers will be assume
 d to be having an affair. Obstreperous raucous yawping is discouraged.\n**
 THIS IS A DOG-PARTICIPANT HIKE.** This event is NOT for those who are unco
 mfortable with the antics of fun-loving dogs. Well trained dogs (you don
 ’t have to yell.) can be 'off-leash'. **'On leash' during the ‘UnRavel
 ling’ stop.** Small (lap)dogs may carpool. Large dogs will drive themsel
 ves.\n**Description**\;\nThere is a large sand beach that is popular in wa
 rm weather. ***Bring gloves. Bring 1 small grocery bag for litter pick-up.
 .***\n**Optional:** swimming in ‘brisk’ water. **Bring an inner tube f
 loat.**\nRemember - hikes led by ‘the Curmudgeon’ tend to have challen
 ging surprises. **Water sprites are mischievous in the Summer.**\nWe will 
 spend up to 2 hrs at the Falls. Pack a camp-chair **there is a large sand 
 beach.** Come prepared to meditate\, practice your Tai-Chi\, **森林浴**
 \, read a book\, prepare a meal\, play a flute.\n**UnRuffle/UnRavel:** To 
 experience a time of quiet in a manner that you feel worthwhile. Démêlez
  votre stress.\nEngage the 5 senses (sight\, smell\, touch\, taste\, heari
 ng)\,\nObserve the movement of the forest & water.\nBreathe the aroma of t
 he air\, water\, plants and forest.\nFeel the texture of the air\, water\,
  trees and plants.\nListening to the sound of air\, water\, critters & bir
 ds\;\nTaste the air of the breezes or soothing snacks.\nAll hikes are at y
 our own risk. You are responsible for your OWN safety and adequate equipme
 nt.\nWaiver: The organizer of this event is a volunteer and not a professi
 onal guide. The function of the organizer is only to organize this event. 
 There are certain risks inherent in any outdoor activity. Each participant
 \, by signing up to attend this event\, agrees to release from liability t
 he leader(s)\, Hendo Fun Friends\, its Partners\, Affiliates\, and members
  for any accident\, injury\, illness\, or personal loss which might occur 
 while participating in this activity or while traveling in any vehicle dur
 ing this trip. **Each participant further agrees to abide by the rules and
  regulations concerning safety\, to follow instructions of the leader(s)\,
  and not to become intentionally separated from the group.** The leader(s)
  also has the right to use any images collected on this trip for recording
  on website photo collections.\ngordie's contact: curmudgeonhiker@gmail.co
 m\n(**before** day of hike): 828.393.0297 (talk & text)\n**Pics: https://w
 ww.flickr.com/photos/146993931@N05/albums**
