SUMMARY:Perry Rudnick Nature Tr\; a Walk
DESCRIPTION:Hendo Fun Friends\n**A WALK IN THE PARK.**\nWe will Tour de Pa
 rks of the area. One at a time.\n**THIS WEEK: Perry Rudnick Nature Tr in K
 ellogg Preserve**\nWe are the Sloth Walking Team: “We will get there whe
 n we get there.”\n**The Curmudgeon will lead this event. Up to 12 ppl** 
 are welcome to join us.\n**https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Bsh_8qxUfDY**\n
 Length: 1.4 mi\; Accum ascent: 100 ft. Walking sticks recommended.\nDrive 
 time: 15 min\n**Limited Parking\; Carpooling necessary.**\nGoogle Map = 
 “Kellogg Nature Trails”\nApprx return time: 12 noon (=1.75hrs)\n**(Thi
 s event is NOT for beginners or those with health or balance issues.)**\n*
 *Optional: Some of us will lunch after the walk.**\nWeather Check: Henders
 onville\, NC.\nCarpool contributions appreciated. $1.00 suggested\nDifficu
 lty: Moderate\; with roots on an earthen tr. **1 very short steep section.
 ** Sturdy shoes suggested. Suitable for almost everyone. NOT suitable for 
 those with balance issues.\nWAITLISTED PEOPLE WILL BE ADDED AS DRIVERS SIG
 N ON.\nI currently have 3 driver(s). (=13ppl)\nWe suggest open windows whi
 le carpooling. Only you know your own health status so judge accordingly i
 f an event may endanger your health or the health of others.\nPlease bring
  an extra pair of shoes to avoid bringing your muddy shoes into the driver
 's car at the end of the hike.\nIncessant prattlers will be assumed to be 
 having an affair. My attempts to quiet the prattlers has failed. This has 
 become a ‘social networking’ event.\n**This is a dog-participant walk.
 ** This event is NOT for those who are uncomfortable with the antics of fu
 n-loving dogs. Dogs are welcome (IF their masters are well trained). 'On l
 eash' rules apply. Small (lap)dogs may carpool. Large dogs will drive them
 selves.\n**DESCRIPTION\;**\nRemember - hikes led by ‘the Curmudgeon’ t
 end to have challenging surprises.\nWood elves are mischievous\; Zip your 
 backpacks tight.\nThe 1.5 mile trail meanders through three distinct ecosy
 stems—trillium and fern wetland\, hardwood forest with rhododendron and 
 mountain laurel\, and wildflower meadow. Various art sculptures are scatte
 red throughout.\nAll walks are at your own risk. You are responsible for y
 our OWN safety and adequate equipment.\nWaiver: The organizer of this even
 t is a volunteer and not a professional guide. The function of the organiz
 er is only to organize this event. There are certain risks inherent in any
  outdoor activity. Each participant\, by signing up to attend this event\,
  agrees to release from liability the leader(s)\, Hendo Fun Friends\, its 
 Partners\, Affiliates\, and members for any accident\, injury\, illness\, 
 or personal loss which might occur while participating in this activity or
  while traveling in any vehicle during this trip. Each participant further
  agrees to abide by the rules and regulations concerning safety\, to follo
 w instructions of the leader(s)\, and not to become intentionally separate
 d from the group. The leader(s) also has the right to use any images colle
 cted on this trip for recording on website photo collections.\ngordie's co
 ntact: CurmudgeonHiker@gmail.com\n(**before** day of hike): 828.393.0297 (
 text only)\n**Pics: https://www.flickr.com/photos/146993931@N05/albums**
